      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/dominion-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "When the railroad bypassed the site, the town was abandoned within months, leaving only a brief boom.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/dominion-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Dominion sits on Wolf Creek in Lipscomb County, near the Oklahoma line, and once vied with Lipscomb for the county seat.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/dominion-tx",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Today Dominion is a master‑planned community covering about 1,500 acres on San Antonio’s northwest side.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
